! AlAs, the same cell as `alas-raman.in`, with an ultrasoft dataset on both
! species: the noncentrosymmetric ultrasoft crystal P94 measures the Kubo
! curvature's moving-overlap term on. Zincblende, so nothing forces the Berry
! curvature to vanish pointwise the way inversion does in silicon, and two
! ultrasoft species, so `S` has a `k` in it.
!
! **It is not a matched control for `alas-raman.in` and must not be read as
! one.** That file is `Al.pz-vbc` and `As.pz-bhs`, norm-conserving LDA at
! `ecutwfc = 10`; these are the PBE ultrasoft `psl` pair and need 25 with a
! dual of 8. So the two runs differ in the functional and the cutoff as well as
! in the dataset, and the pair bounds the size of an effect rather than
! isolating one. Every conclusion P94 draws from this cell rests on this column
! alone -- how far `Omega` moves when `dS/dk` is zeroed, against how far the two
! curvature methods are apart on the *same* run.
!
! The cell, positions, k-grid and `nosym`/`noinv` are `alas-raman.in`'s.
 &control
    calculation = 'scf'
 /
 &system
    ibrav = 2, celldm(1) = 10.575, nat = 2, ntyp = 2,
    ecutwfc = 25.0, ecutrho = 200.0
    nosym = .true.
    noinv = .true.
 /
 &electrons
    conv_thr = 1.0d-10
    mixing_beta = 0.7
 /
ATOMIC_SPECIES
 Al  26.98  Al.pbe-n-rrkjus_psl.1.0.0.UPF
 As  74.92  As.pbe-n-rrkjus_psl.1.0.0.UPF
ATOMIC_POSITIONS (alat)
 Al 0.00 0.00 0.00
 As 0.25 0.25 0.25
K_POINTS (automatic)
 4 4 4 0 0 0
